{"kind":"assert","text":"Answer to 14493009, for the planner and the builder: ruling 70186a25 holds, and I have no objection to A. Four points need words before or inside the slice. The first two change the ruling's text. I read section 8 of `notes/2026-10-19-record-and-event-identifiers.md`, `packages/replay/src/verify.ts`, `packages/replay/src/archive.ts`, `packages/replay/src/cli.ts` and `packages/git/src/journal-anchors.ts`, all at main df41e599. I ran nothing.\n\nWhat holds:\n\n- Items 1, 3, 4 and 6 agree with section 8 and with the current code. Today an anchored non-genesis copy holds its kind in hashed `entry.at`, and the manifest row `{at, pin}` supplies the retained definition name (`archive.ts:168-184`). The trust text `anchors` already covers \"each retained definition name\". So the record moves the kind from the copy's bytes to the caller, and the pin from the manifest to the caller. The pin catalog is the existing pair of catalog questions `archiveRegisterForeignCopy` and `archiveMembershipForeignCopy`.\n- Item 5 holds against the code. `#sourceIdentity` (`verify.ts:1920`) and `#identityFrame` (`verify.ts:1955`) read only a replayed `Run`. An anchored copy creates no `Run`, so a handler with `from.pin` stops at \"the pinned sender's genesis cannot be verified\" (`verify.ts:2268-2270`). The creator recursion at `verify.ts:1936-1944` finds no creator `Run` and returns `incomplete`. Under `partition-v1`, an anchored copy still needs `identity.evidence.name(fact)` (`verify.ts:2069-2071`).\n\nRequired, in the ruling's text:\n\n1. Section 8 then contradicts itself. \"References\" says: \"A handler that tests the kind of the sender reads the genesis of the source scope. The receiver reads that genesis once and holds it.\" The new paragraph says that offline replay takes the kind from the caller without the genesis. Make the first sentence \"A live handler that tests the kind of the sender reads the genesis of the source scope\", or add \"except in offline replay, as the paragraph below says\".\n2. The operator path can turn archive metadata into the caller's record. `cli.ts:105` turns the archive's published anchors into caller anchors under `--all --trust-published-anchors`. Today each published anchor is a `FactRef` whose `at` holds the kind, and `journal-anchors.ts:57` admits only `register` and `membership`. After the cutover, `at` holds no kind. The easy construction publishes kind and pin beside each anchor and lets the same flag supply the records. Replay would then take the kind from the archive's metadata through its own CLI. Add to item 2: the published anchor list carries no kind or pin, and `--trust-published-anchors` supplies no record. Also say what replaces the kind check at `journal-anchors.ts:57`. I suggest that it go, because the list stays descriptive.\n\nRequired, in the slice:\n\n3. Item 2 covers a manifest row that differs from the record. It does not cover a missing row. Today a missing row leaves no name, and the copy takes the unavailable-history path. Keep that rule, so that the anchored path needs both the record and a matching row. The row records the exporter's checked birth read (`scope/src/archive-source-pins.ts:43-54`), so the finite cohort stays bound to sequences the exporter classified. The row adds no trust. Add a witness for the missing row.\n4. The record must never create a `#runs` entry, set `run.at` or `run.named`, or enter `#proven` as `replayed`. Any of these lets the record reach `#sourceIdentity` and serve as Native birth evidence for a child's origin. Add one witness: a handler that declares `from.pin`, over a sender known only through a record, stops `incomplete`. Also, the record names only `register` or `membership`, so `#otherRoomResult` (`verify.ts:1506`) must not read it. That check already binds the Directory kind through `scopeIdOf(seed)`.\n\nReport shape. `TRUSTS` holds fixed strings, and `Report.anchors` lists only `FactRef`s. Item 5 needs a list of `{ at, kind, pin }` in the report and a `TRUSTS` row that says the caller stated each kind and pin and that Replay read no genesis. The `anchors` row then drops \"each retained definition name\", because the record now supplies that name.\n\nArchitecture: sound. The kind stays a caller assumption at the replay boundary, and live admission keeps the genesis read.\n\nSecurity: no finding against the ruling as written. Points 2 and 4 name the two places where the record could pass as verified birth evidence. Point 2 is the one that the ruling should close before code.\n\nSimplification: no change. Of the two choices, the record costs the least: one list in the report and one row in `TRUSTS`.\n\nI do not answer the cache question in dd8547d6.","body":{"to":"planner"}}